\section{Not circular}{

Every density, including \code{reference_density}, is validated by the
\emph{same} complete procedure (\code{\link[=compare_neighborhoods]{compare_neighborhoods()}} +
\code{\link[=summarize_comparison]{summarize_comparison()}} + \code{\link[=comparison_to_edges]{comparison_to_edges()}}) -- there is no
separate, cheaper approximation for the profile grid. \code{strength} never
reads any density's \code{q.value}; it is built entirely from the
deterministic mid-p rank (\code{.coexpr_reciprocal_midp()}), a quantity
\code{reference}'s q-values do not use and do not feed. \code{density_support} at
each density is that density's own independently BH-corrected
significance call (\code{type != "ns"}), never a reused decision from
\code{reference_density} or from any other density in the grid; the fraction
of the grid supporting a call is reported purely descriptively (as
recurrence, following Curci et al. 2022), never pooled into a combined
p-value across the (mutually dependent) densities. \code{reference} is
additionally computed with the package's usual randomized-p pi0
estimator (\code{pi0_method = "randomized"}, needs \code{seed}); every other
density in the grid uses the deterministic Storey estimator
(\code{pi0_method = "storey"}) so the profile itself never draws from the
RNG.
